{title: No, Not One}
{artist: Johnson Oatman Jr. / George C. Hugg}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: F}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: no-not-one.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (No_Not_One-No_Not_One) and the Cyber Hymnal score (97% of syllables agree)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]There’s not a friend like the [Bb]lowly [F]Jesus,
[F]No, not [C]one! [F]No, [C7]not [F]one!
[F]None else could heal all our [Bb]soul’s dis[F]eases,
[F]No, not [C]one! [Am]No, [C7]not [F]one!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Jesus knows all about our struggles,
[F]He will guide till the day is [C]done;
[F]There’s not a friend like the [Bb]lowly [F]Jesus,
[F]No, not [C]one! [Am]No, [C7]not [F]one!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]No friend like Him is so [Bb]high and [F]holy,
[F]No, not [C]one! [F]No, [C7]not [F]one!
[F]And yet no friend is so [Bb]meek and [F]lowly,
[F]No, not [C]one! [Am]No, [C7]not [F]one!__[C]__[F]__[Bb]__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]There’s not an hour that He [Bb]is not [F]near us,
[F]No, not [C]one! [F]No, [C7]not [F]one!
[F]No night so dark but His [Bb]love can [F]cheer us,
[F]No, not [C]one! [Am]No, [C7]not [F]one!__[C]__[F]__[Bb]__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Did ever saint find this [Bb]friend for[F]sake him?
[F]No, not [C]one! [F]No, [C7]not [F]one!
[F]Or sinner find that He [Bb]would not [F]take him?
[F]No, not [C]one! [Am]No, [C7]not [F]one!__[C]__[F]__[Bb]__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[F]Was ever a gift like the [Bb]Savior [F]given?
[F]No, not [C]one! [F]No, [C7]not [F]one!
[F]Will He refuse us a [Bb]home in [F]Heaven?
[F]No, not [C]one! [Am]No, [C7]not [F]one!__[C]__[F]__[Bb]__[F]__[C]__[Am]__[C7]__[F]__
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
